UFW on Tenko
============

Installation leaves the firewall and ufw.service disabled. Configure access
before enabling it, especially on a remote machine. For SSH on TCP port 22:

    sudo ufw allow 22/tcp
    sudo ufw enable
    sudo systemctl enable ufw.service
    sudo ufw status verbose

Use your actual SSH port and allow any other required services first.
The systemd unit restores enabled UFW rules before network setup at boot.
Enabling the unit alone does not enable filtering: /etc/ufw/ufw.conf must
also contain ENABLED=yes, which "ufw enable" sets.

    sudo ufw disable
    sudo systemctl disable ufw.service

Configuration and administrator-managed rules live in /etc/default/ufw and
/etc/ufw. RPM upgrades preserve local edits. Helper scripts live in
/usr/lib/ufw, and pristine rule templates in /usr/share/ufw/iptables.
IPv6 support is enabled in /etc/default/ufw.

Use UFW as the firewall manager instead of simultaneously running an
iptables, nftables or firewalld service. Container networking and other
software can also manage netfilter rules; review their interaction before
enabling or reloading UFW. See ufw(8) and ufw-framework(8).
